# The build context is this directory, and the Dockerfile copies nothing out of
# it: every byte in the image comes from apt and PyPI. So the context is the
# Dockerfile and nothing else — the page beside it and the smoke test that runs
# the built image are for readers and for CI, and neither belongs in a layer or
# in the tarball the daemon is handed.
#
# One exception, and it still puts no byte in the image: `await_index.py` is
# bind-mounted into the install step, so it has to be in the context the
# daemon is handed. Excluded, the build fails before any wait with
# `"/await_index.py": not found`, which is how CI found this.
*
!Dockerfile
!await_index.py
